  "notes": "Governmental activities and funds are modified cash basis (basis=cash); business-type activities are accrual (net position). Governmental funds use Total Governmental Funds column (p4, p5); no transfers, debt proceeds or other financing printed as actual. Beginning cash = prior year total fund balance (no liabilities). Keno fund only appears in the basic statements (interest 28), no detail schedule. Balance sheet uses government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (mixes modified cash governmental and accrual business-type). Business-type receipts/disbursements from Total column of proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Net Position (p9); business-type expenses listed by object so function set to utilities (Electric, Water, Sewer, Nursing Home combined). No single business-type receipts total printed; computed. proprietary cash flow statement (pp10-11) not recorded because the entity is cash basis, not GAAP. General Fund detail taken from the more detailed combining departments schedule (p14-15), which sums to General Fund totals; the General Fund budgetary comparison schedule (p12) is not recorded to avoid double counting. Department functions: Administrative = general government, Police/Fire = public safety, Park/Library = environment and leisure (culture/recreation), Dump = public works. Salaries and benefits are combined in one printed line. Component unit (Library Foundation) excluded. Read pages 1-15 of 15 Nursing Home Fund column's repairs (4,536) and depreciation (8,533) split out of the Total column lines as hospital/health care (p9)."
}